{
  "_comment": "Drop this at .claude/project.json (rename, remove _comment). All keys are optional — skills skip steps gracefully when keys are missing. See README.md for which skill reads which key.",

  "test": {
    "_comment": "Commands used by /test-check, and /sdlc. Any missing key is skipped.",
    "unit": "pytest tests/ -v --tb=short",
    "frontend": "cd web && pnpm test --run",
    "e2e": "npx playwright test --reporter=json",
    "_e2e_extras": "The next three keys tune `/test-check --loop` and the e2e-test-runner agent. All optional.",
    "e2e_max_fix_loops": 3,
    "e2e_patterns_file": ".claude/e2e-patterns.md",
    "e2e_rerun_failed_only": true
  },

  "logs": {
    "_comment": "Used by /test-check and the log-audit script. {service} and {tail} are substituted.",
    "command": "docker compose logs {service} --tail={tail}",
    "services": ["api", "web", "worker"]
  },

  "stack": {
    "_comment": "Optional. How to bring this project's runnable stack up for MANUAL verification — the hand-off at the end of /sdlc, or an ad-hoc 'get it running so I can click through'. Every key optional; a missing key means that action is unavailable and skills say so instead of guessing. These are NEVER run automatically: a skill may print the command, and only runs one when you ask.",
    "up": "docker compose up -d --build",
    "_rebuild_comment": "Clean rebuild — used when a dependency manifest changed (see discipline.deploy_delta_globs), where a plain restart would silently run stale code.",
    "rebuild": "docker compose up -d --build --force-recreate",
    "_url_comment": "Where to look once it is up. Printed in the hand-off so you don't have to remember the port.",
    "url": "http://localhost:3000"
  },

  "eval": {
    "_comment": "Used by /test-check step 6 and /sdlc Stage 3.",
    "_runner_options": "Two patterns: (1) consumer-resident (setup.sh copied scripts/ into this repo) — use 'bash scripts/py.sh scripts/eval-runner.py'; (2) plugin-resident (setup.sh ran with --no-copy-scripts) — use 'bash /absolute/path/to/brainstorm-toolkit/scripts/py.sh /absolute/path/to/brainstorm-toolkit/scripts/eval-runner.py'. Plugin-resident keeps shared infra in one place and benefits from plugin updates without re-running setup.",
    "runner": "bash scripts/py.sh scripts/eval-runner.py",
    "features_dir": "evals/",
    "_thresholds_comment": "Optional. Without this block, eval-runner uses binary pass/fail (any failure = FAIL). min_pass_rate is the only enforced threshold; 0.98 is the ratchet target for prod-bound repos.",
    "thresholds": {
      "min_pass_rate": 0.85,
      "_recommended_for_prod_bound_repos": {
        "min_pass_rate": 0.98
      }
    }
  },

  "_python_comment": "Optional. The Python interpreter THIS machine actually has, used by scripts/py.sh, which every shipped command routes through. Set it to whatever is true for your OS — 'python3' on most Linux/macOS, 'python' or an absolute path like 'C:\\\\Python311\\\\python.exe' on Windows. WHY THIS KEY EXISTS: there is no portable token. On Windows 'python3' is usually a Microsoft Store STUB that resolves on PATH, prints 'Python was not found', opens the Store and exits non-zero — so a command hardcoding it is broken there; 'python' is absent on stock macOS and on Debian/Ubuntu without python-is-python3, so hardcoding that is broken elsewhere. Omit this key and py.sh probes python3 → python → py, taking the first that actually RUNS (not merely resolves — the stub passes a PATH check and then fails). A configured value that does not run is reported and falls back to the probe, so a stale entry cannot brick every skill. $BRAINSTORM_PYTHON overrides this.",
  "python": "python3",

  "gotchas_file": "GOTCHAS.md",
  "main_branch": "main",

  "_coauthor_trailer_comment": "Optional, default false. When true, every commit message this toolkit writes or suggests ends with a 'Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>' trailer (blank line before it), and so does any PR body a future step authors. Read by /task (the only skill that runs git commit, and only when you ask) and by /sdlc's Stage 6 suggested-commit hand-off (which prints the message for you to run -- /sdlc never commits). Absent or false = no trailer, ever. Default is false because attribution is a disclosure choice, not a default, and some DCO / commit-lint setups reject unrecognized trailers. /repo-onboarding asks and records your answer here.",
  "coauthor_trailer": false,

  "modules": ["api", "web", "worker"],

  "_models_comment": "EVERY model-tier choice lives here -- there is no CLI flag; canonical contract: skills/sdlc/templates/models.md. Each dispatch role has its own key (a string tier haiku|sonnet|opus, or a per-sub-role map where noted); a repo that sets nothing runs every role at its built-in default. TWO INDEPENDENT AXES. Axis 1 (every role key except code_review*/planner) is bounded by models.cap, a ceiling that only LOWERS and is absent = no ceiling. Axis 2 (code_review*; values haiku|sonnet|opus|fable) is NOT governed by the cap, and an explicit code_review value is always the dispatched value. 'planner' is a THIRD kind, on NEITHER axis. Recommended pairing: Sonnet implements (models.implement), Opus reviews (pipeline.review_fix.enabled: true + models.code_review: \"opus\").",
  "models": {
    "cap": "opus",
    "_cap_comment": "Optional; absent = NO ceiling (the built-in defaults are already Sonnet-first, so nothing is lowered unless you set this). A CEILING that only ever LOWERS a per-role tier on the haiku < sonnet < opus ladder: effective = min(models.<role> ?? built-in default, cap). It never raises a tier and never touches Axis 2 (code_review*) or planner. Example value shown caps nothing below opus; set \"sonnet\" to hold every fan-out to Sonnet.",
    "sanity": null,
    "_sanity_comment": "Optional, default null (= built-in per-focus defaults: paths haiku, completeness sonnet, gotchas sonnet). Controls the plan pre-flight focuses (/sdlc Stage 1.5, never gated; /brainstorm vet-light uses the same three focus names). String (haiku|sonnet|opus, replaces every focus) or MAP (e.g. {\"completeness\": \"opus\"}; a focus missing from the map keeps its own default). Invalid value -> that focus's built-in default.",
    "implement": "sonnet",
    "_implement_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the /sdlc implementer, the Stage 2a decomposer, every Stage 2b lane (one tier for all lanes) and the Stage 5.9 cleanup-apply agent. Recommended pairing: Sonnet implements, Opus reviews (pipeline.review_fix.enabled: true + models.code_review: \"opus\").",
    "fix": "sonnet",
    "_fix_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the Stage 5 fix-loop agent. pipeline.fix_loop.escalate_last still raises only the last iteration one rung (to opus at most), then capped.",
    "validate": "sonnet",
    "_validate_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the Stage 5 plan-conformance-validator.",
    "test_runner": "haiku",
    "_test_runner_comment": "Optional, default \"haiku\". Controls test-runner agent dispatches (/sdlc Stage 5, /test-check). The dispatch passes this as an explicit model, which outranks the agent's own frontmatter pin.",
    "e2e": "sonnet",
    "_e2e_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls e2e-test-runner dispatches (/sdlc Stage 5, /test-check --loop), including any in-loop escalation -- raise it here instead.",
    "cleanup": "sonnet",
    "_cleanup_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the /sdlc Stage 5.9 cleanup lenses.",
    "reassess": "sonnet",
    "_reassess_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the /sdlc Stage 6 action-items reassess agent.",
    "brainstorm": "sonnet",
    "_brainstorm_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls /brainstorm explorers, the vet-deep stress-test and vet-ultra agents.",
    "brainstorm_team": "sonnet",
    "_brainstorm_team_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the six /brainstorm-team teammates.",
    "dead_code_review": null,
    "_dead_code_review_comment": "Optional, default null (= {server: sonnet, client: sonnet, data: sonnet, docs: haiku, scripts: haiku}). Controls the /dead-code-review lenses. String (every lens) or MAP keyed server|client|data|docs|scripts; a lens missing from the map keeps its default.",
    "repo_health": null,
    "_repo_health_comment": "Optional, default null (= each check's built-in tier: the mechanical checks stay haiku, rules-drift sonnet). Controls the /repo-health agent checks. String (every check) or a MAP keyed by check name; a check missing from the map keeps its default.",
    "docstring_sync": "sonnet",
    "_docstring_sync_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\". Controls the /docstring-sync triage and rewrite agents.",
    "planner": "opus",
    "_planner_comment": "Optional, default \"opus\". One of haiku|sonnet|opus|fable. ADVISORY ONLY -- a session-model RECOMMENDATION for /brainstorm and /brainstorm-team's planning conversation, which runs on your host session model rather than a sub-agent. On NEITHER model axis: models.cap never lowers it, and it never governs a dispatch. Printed once per session, verbatim: 'Planning runs on your session model. Recommended: <planner> -- switch before the clarifying rounds if you aren't on it.' Never detects the host model. An unrecognized value falls through to the default. See skills/sdlc/templates/models.md 'A third kind'.",
    "code_review": "opus",
    "_code_review_comment": "Optional, default \"opus\" (Axis 2: never capped). Controls the /sdlc Stage 5.7 review lenses, verify and fix-planner. Stage 5.7 runs only when pipeline.review_fix.enabled is true. Values haiku|sonnet|opus|fable. If it resolves to the implementer's tier (models.implement) the run is marked independence: degraded -- findings surfaced, never auto-fixed.",
    "code_review_second_pass": "sonnet",
    "_code_review_second_pass_comment": "Optional, default \"sonnet\" (Axis 2: never capped). Controls the Stage 5.7 second-pass reviewer; only read when agents.code_review_passes is 2."
  },
  "_agents_comment": "How MANY agents each fan-out stage dispatches. Cost scales roughly linearly -- one agent (or reviewer call) per entry. Unrecognized entries are ignored with one warning; the lists are deliberately open so a repo can add its own. See skills/sdlc/templates/models.md.",
  "agents": {
    "sanity_focuses": ["paths", "completeness", "gotchas"],
    "code_review_lenses": ["correctness", "plan-alignment", "config-env-docs", "security"],
    "code_review_max_lenses": 4,
    "_code_review_max_lenses_comment": "Optional, default 4 (= today's behavior, so this key is inert until changed). Caps HOW MANY Stage 5.7 lenses fan out; code_review_lenses above picks WHICH. Applied AFTER circuit-breaker demotion, truncating in list order -- so 1 keeps 'correctness', the highest-yield lens. Set 1 for a single-reviewer run without needing the lens names. NOTE: each lens is one call at the REVIEWER model (models.code_review, default opus, cap-exempt), so this knob -- not models.cap -- is what bounds review-stage cost. Any non-integer or non-positive value falls through to 4.",
    "code_review_passes": 1,
    "code_review_max_fix_loops": 3,
    "decompose_min_tasks": 6,
    "_decompose_min_tasks_comment": "Optional. Stage 2 fans out into per-surface lanes only when surfaces>=2 AND (task_count>=this OR len(files_to_change)>=agents.decompose_min_files) AND the file sets are disjoint. Default 6.",
    "decompose_min_files": 12,
    "_decompose_min_files_comment": "Optional. The OR partner of decompose_min_tasks above -- catches a small step count spanning a large file count (e.g. 4 steps across ~20 files) that task_count alone would route to a single agent. Default 12.",
    "cleanup_lenses": ["over-engineering", "docstring-currency"],
    "_cleanup_lenses_comment": "Optional, default both (= the array above). Which Stage 5.9 cleanup lenses fan out -- see skills/sdlc/templates/stage-5.9-cleanup.md. An unrecognized entry is ignored with one warning.",
    "cleanup_max_lenses": 2,
    "_cleanup_max_lenses_comment": "Optional, default 2 (= today's behavior, so this key is inert until changed). Caps HOW MANY Stage 5.9 lenses fan out; cleanup_lenses above picks WHICH. Truncates in list order, same convention as code_review_max_lenses. Any non-integer or non-positive value falls through to 2; never 0."
  },

  "migrations": {
    "_comment": "Optional. Read by /repo-health Check 6 (static migration drift). Omit entirely if the project has no migrations — the check self-skips.",
    "dir": "backend/migrations",
    "_applied_check_comment": "A shell command (or SQL via your DB CLI) that prints the highest applied migration version. /repo-health compares it to the highest file in 'dir' and warns if the repo is ahead (merged-but-unapplied). Without it, the check reports 'applied state unknown' rather than connecting to a DB.",
    "applied_check": "psql \"$DATABASE_URL\" -tAc \"select max(version) from schema_migrations\""
  },

  "discipline": {
    "_comment": "Optional. Tunes the self-enforcing gates. All keys have defaults; omit the block to accept them. Project-agnostic — gates self-skip when their surface is absent.",
    "staleness_hours": 24,
    "_globs_comment": "Override the changed-files-gate surface globs (see skills/sdlc/templates/changed-files-gate.md). Defaults cover the common cases; set these only for non-standard layouts.",
    "frontend_globs": ["**/*.tsx", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.vue", "**/*.svelte", "**/*.css", "**/*.scss"],
    "backend_globs": ["**/*.py", "**/*.go", "**/*.rb", "**/*.java", "**/*.ts"],
    "data_globs": ["**/migrations/**", "**/schema/**", "**/models/**", "**/*.sql"],
    "docs_globs": ["**/*.md", "docs/**"],
    "_deploy_delta_comment": "Dependency manifests/lockfiles/Dockerfiles. When the diff touches one, /sdlc flags 'rebuild required (not restart)' in the Stage 7 report + checklist — code committed != running env reflects it.",
    "deploy_delta_globs": ["requirements.txt", "pyproject.toml", "poetry.lock", "package.json", "package-lock.json", "pnpm-lock.yaml", "yarn.lock", "go.mod", "Cargo.toml", "Gemfile.lock", "Dockerfile", "**/Dockerfile"],
    "_memory_index_comment": "Optional path to a REPO-LOCAL memory/knowledge index for /repo-health Check 8. Leave unset to skip — the check NEVER reads the user-global ~/.claude memory dir.",
    "memory_index": null
  },

  "pipeline": {
    "_comment": "Optional. Knobs read by /sdlc. Most keys default to false/unset.",
    "skip_secret_scan": false,
    "_poka_yoke_comment": "Claude-only. When true, /repo-onboarding writes a PreToolUse hook to .claude/settings.json that blocks Write/Edit when a likely secret is in the payload. Enabling this key alone does NOT install the hook — see AGENTS.md 'Hooks (Claude-only)' for the settings.json schema. Copilot consumers gain nothing from this key (no PreToolUse equivalent); rely on the Stage 6 gitleaks scan instead.",
    "poka_yoke": false,
    "_enforce_cap_comment": "Claude-only, default false. When true, the PreToolUse(Agent) hook scripts/hooks/enforce-model-cap.sh (wired by setup.sh / the plugin) makes models.cap deterministic: a dispatch whose model ranks above the cap is rewritten to the cap, and a dispatch that omits model gets the cap unless its agent definition pins a tier. Dispatches whose description starts 'review:' (the Axis 2 reviewer) are exempt. With enforcement on, models.cap is policy: a role you set above it (e.g. models.implement: \"opus\" under cap \"sonnet\") is clamped, so raise or remove models.cap instead. A repo with no models.cap is never rewritten. Each rewrite is shown to you as a systemMessage; it never blocks.",
    "enforce_cap": false,
    "_stop_gate_comment": "Claude/Codex only (Copilot gets no wiring), default \"off\". Set \"tests\" to make the Stop hook scripts/hooks/stop-gate.sh re-run test.unit whenever an /sdlc run's envelope is in_progress and block the handoff (decision:block) on a red result, bounded by pipeline.loop.max_hops consecutive failures before it stands down. Inert (zero output) unless stop_gate is \"tests\" AND an in_progress envelope exists AND test.unit is configured. It never blocks when test.unit is missing on PATH, and it stands down for stop_hook_active or a pending .claude/.next-action sentinel so it is never a second Stop-hook blocker -- see docs/SEAM.md.",
    "stop_gate": "off",
    "_stop_gate_timeout_comment": "Seconds before stop-gate.sh gives up on test.unit (timeout(1)). Default 300.",
    "stop_gate_timeout": 300,

    "scope": {
      "_comment": "Optional. Stage 0's scope gate for /sdlc -- caps how much of an oversized plan-file run one invocation takes. Task id / range / ad-hoc / --queue inputs are already bounded and never pass through this gate.",
      "max_steps_per_run": 8,
      "_max_steps_per_run_comment": "Fallback step-count cut, used only when the plan has no '#### Phase N' headers to cut on. When it does, the gate takes the lowest phase with open rows and parks the rest whole, regardless of this number -- it never splits a sequentially-dependent chain to hit a count. Default 8. Pass --no-scope-gate on a single run to force whole-plan execution instead of changing this."
    },

    "output": {
      "_comment": "Optional. Stage-narration verbosity for /sdlc. DEFAULT IS 'quiet' -- this block exists to opt OUT, not in. Narration is re-read by every later turn in the same session, so it compounds. Detail is never lost: it is already written to the stage sidecars under .claude/pipeline/<slug>/stage-outputs/. MEASURED CAVEAT: on an audited run narration was only ~2% of main-thread tokens -- do this for signal-to-noise, not for savings. The real drivers were shell traffic (~53%) and the orchestrator writing files into its own context instead of delegating (~18%).",
      "verbosity": "quiet",
      "_verbosity_comment": "'quiet' (default) | 'normal'. Under 'quiet' each stage prints ONE status line (stage, verdict, model line) and the run ends with one summary table. Even under 'quiet' the per-dispatch 'model: <tier> (cap: <cap>)' line, every gate verdict, and the 'Next:' seam line are ALWAYS printed -- nothing automated enforces the first (validate_skills.py only soft-warns that a fan-out skill references the models contract; it never checks the line is printed), so that instruction is the whole enforcement surface."
    },

    "context": {
      "_comment": "Optional. Run-cost reporting. There is deliberately NO mid-run context threshold: a warning fired partway through a run is a lagging indicator (the tokens are already spent) and arrives mid-plan, where clearing is explicitly unsafe (docs/LOOP-HYGIENE.md). The report below fires ONCE, at terminal state, as a LEADING indicator for the next plan you write.",
      "cost_report": "on",
      "_cost_report_comment": "'on' (default) | 'off'. When a run reaches complete/failed/paused, scripts/hooks/run-cost-report.sh prints turns, average context, peak context, cache-read total and a rough spend figure. COSTS ZERO MODEL TOKENS: it is emitted as `systemMessage`, which the hook contract shows to the human and never injects into the model's context. Never reimplement it via hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext -- a cost report that costs tokens defeats itself. Set 'off' to silence."
    },

    "fix_loop": {
      "_comment": "Optional, OFF by default. Stage 5's shared 3-iteration fix budget (skills/sdlc/templates/fix-loop.md). Excluded entirely from Stage 5.7/5.8, which has its own separate budget and whose reviewer axis (models.code_review) is not on this ladder.",
      "escalate_last": false,
      "_escalate_last_comment": "When true, ONLY the final iteration of Stage 5's shared fix-loop budget dispatches its fix agent at min(stage_tier + 1, effective_cap) on the haiku < sonnet < opus ladder, printing 'model: <tier> (cap: <cap>, escalated)' in place of the ordinary dispatch line. With models.cap: \"sonnet\", min(sonnet + 1, sonnet) is a no-op -- nothing changes. With no cap (or \"opus\") iterations 1-2 dispatch at models.fix (default Sonnet) and the last iteration dispatches one rung up, at Opus. Without this key, every retry stays on the same tier by design -- a fix loop is not a place to guess your way up the ladder silently. Copilot/Codex (no sub-agent seam): when true, the PAUSED block adds 'Escalate: set models.fix to opus in .claude/project.json, then --resume' instead of escalating inline. scripts/hooks/enforce-model-cap.sh needs no change for this -- an escalation that stays within the cap is never rewritten."
    },

    "review_fix": {
      "_comment": "Optional, OFF by default. Adversarial Review->Fix stage (Stage 5.7 review / Stage 5.8 fix loop) for /sdlc -- an N-lens adversarial review + fix loop that runs after Stage 5, before the Stage 6 hand-off. Default reviewer model 'opus' (see skills/sdlc/templates/models.md; the reviewer model itself lives at models.code_review). Omit this whole block to accept the defaults below (stage stays OFF). OPT-IN, PERMANENTLY: there is no default-on flip, planned or shipped. An explicit enabled:true here is required to activate the stage; omitted, absent, or enabled:false all mean OFF.",
      "enabled": false,
      "mode": "interactive",
      "_mode_comment": "One of 'interactive' (default: each confirmed finding's fix spec is presented for approve/edit/skip, then the run pauses before Stage 6 with anything remaining surfaced), 'auto' (auto-approve every confirmed auto_fixable:true finding, bounded by agents.code_review_max_fix_loops -- design-decision findings, auto_fixable:false, are NEVER auto-approved in any mode), 'off' (report only, Stage 5.8 does not run). There is no confidence or consecutive-approval throttle: the auto_fixable rubric and the loop budget are the whole bound.",
      "_cost_bound_comment": "Diff size is NOT bounded here -- every lens reviews the whole diff. The levers that exist are agents.code_review_lenses and agents.code_review_max_lenses (fan-out width). See skills/sdlc/templates/models.md for the removed-key record."
    },

    "cleanup": {
      "_comment": "Optional, OFF by default. Stage 5.9 cleanup pass for /sdlc -- an opt-in, quality-only lens fan-out (over-engineering, docstring-currency) scoped to implement.json data.files_changed[], that runs after Stage 5.8 and only once Stage 5 is green with real test evidence. See skills/sdlc/templates/stage-5.9-cleanup.md. Bug-hunting is out of scope by design (that's Stage 5.7's correctness lens), and this stage never calls /simplify (a Claude Code CLI built-in, absent on Copilot/Codex). Omit this whole block to accept the defaults below (stage stays OFF). OPT-IN, PERMANENTLY: an explicit --cleanup flag or an explicit enabled:true here is required to activate the stage; omitted, absent, or enabled:false all mean OFF, and --no-cleanup always wins OFF.",
      "enabled": false,
      "mode": "interactive",
      "_mode_comment": "One of 'interactive' (default: the full findings list is shown once, then a single confirm to apply the safe_to_apply findings -- not per-finding approve/edit/skip), 'auto' (apply every confirmed safe_to_apply finding without prompting), 'off' (report only, nothing is applied -- git diff is identical before and after this stage). A finding is safe_to_apply only if it is a deletion, a docstring edit, or a rename with every call site named; anything else is report-only regardless of mode."
    },

    "loop": {
      "_comment": "Optional. Knobs for the --queue backlog loop (/sdlc --queue), the L9 auto-continue Stop hook, and the batch-handoff runner (scripts/loop-runner.sh). All optional.",
      "max_items": 5,
      "_max_items_comment": "Max items one /sdlc --queue invocation consumes before it stops (the [N] arg overrides). Default 5.",
      "batch_size": 5,
      "_batch_size_comment": "scripts/loop-runner.sh ONLY: items per FRESH headless process before context is reset (a clean completed-item boundary, never mid-plan). 5-10 is the useful range -- large enough to amortize the per-process baseline, small enough to cap growth. Resolves: --queue X flag > batch_size > max_items > 5. See docs/LOOP-HYGIENE.md.",
      "max_hops": 5,
      "_max_hops_comment": "Auto-continue (L9) hop budget: max self-continue chain length before the Stop hook parks. Default 5.",
      "auto_continue": false,
      "_auto_continue_comment": "Claude/Codex only, OFF by default. When true, the Stop hook EXECUTES a single non-confirm .next-action sentinel (decision:block) instead of only printing it, so the loop self-advances. Never chains a confirm:true action; bounded by max_hops."
    },

    "action_items": {
      "_comment": "Optional. A generated 'what runs when' file (ACTION_ITEMS.md) built from TASKS.md by scripts/close-tasks.sh waves: a now wave and a next wave, grouped by lane. /sdlc Stage 6 regenerates it after closing rows, /sdlc --queue selects from the now wave, and /sdlc-status prints one line from it. Derived and gitignored; edit TASKS.md, never the file.",
      "enabled": false,
      "_enabled_comment": "false is a VETO: the feature is off whatever files exist. true turns it on. When absent it is on only if the file below exists AND its first line is the generated banner ('<!-- generated — edit TASKS.md'). Read both keys first -- never test the default name when file is set (bash scripts/close-tasks.sh waves --gate does this). A hand-written file never opts a repo in and is never overwritten, even with enabled true. The file path and the check resolve against the TASKS.md directory, not the cwd.",
      "file": "ACTION_ITEMS.md",
      "reassess": false,
      "_reassess_comment": "Default false. When true AND the open-row set changed since the last run, Stage 6 dispatches ONE Sonnet agent that proposes _after: / _lane: / _conflicts: row tags the file-and-phase rules cannot see. Every proposal needs a verbatim evidence quote from the plan; scripts/close-tasks.sh tag is the only writer, and a proposal whose quote is not found is dropped, never applied. Only has effect when action items are enabled."
    },

    "tasks": {
      "_comment": "Optional. How /sdlc Stage 6 closes TASKS.md rows.",
      "close_in_place": false,
      "_close_in_place_comment": "Default false: a closed row moves to ## Done. true: scripts/close-tasks.sh close --in-place flips it to [x] (with its completion stamp) where it stands, so TASKS.md:N line citations stay valid; moved[] is empty."
    }
  }
}
